// CROWN refinement (H4·D, 2026-10-01): the sound dual of the element leak —
// `first` applies its list's element at 5, which proves `inv`'s
// precondition outright, so no guard is owed and `!Trap` holds. The element
// is taken by a list pattern, which tests its length: an index `fs[0]` over
// a parameter is an open bounds claim and performs Trap (TRAP, 2026-10-06).
type Positive = Int where 0 < self

fn inv(n: Positive) = 100 / n

fn first(fs) = match fs {
  [f, ..._] => f(5),
  _ => 0,
}

fn main() with !Trap = first([inv])
